-- chem/charge.cub — the electric interaction between charges, exactly, as a count of spanning trees.
-- In loop quantum gravity with matter (Thiemann, QSD V, 1997; Bianchi, Han, Magliaro, Perini, Rovelli and
-- Wieland, "Spinfoam fermions", 2010; Lewandowski and Zhang, 2021) a fermion sits at the open end of a
-- Faraday line of the spin network, and the Maxwell field is a U(1) flux carried on the network's lines;
-- Gauss's law at each vertex says the flux leaving it equals the charge sitting there. The electric
-- energy of the field a pair of opposite unit charges holds between them is, in the Gaussian (non-compact)
-- theory, the minimum of the flux's energy over all fluxes obeying Gauss's law (Thomson's principle), and
-- Kirchhoff (1847) gave that minimum as a ratio of two counts: the spanning trees of the network with the
